{"name":"Cupcake Rose","hex":"#e6c7b7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cupcake","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small cake baked in a usually paper container shaped like a cup, often with icing on top.","An attractive young woman."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To flirt; to talk or act amorously or intimately.","To flirt with; to talk or act amorously or intimately to."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cupcake"},{"term":"rose","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shrub of the genus Rosa, with red, pink, white or yellow flowers.","A flower of the rose plant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make rose-colored; to redden or flush.","To perfume, as with roses."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rose"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cupcake","blocks":[{"text":"A cupcake, fairy cake (BrE), patty cake (AuE), or bun (IrE) is a small cake designed to serve one person, which may be baked in a small thin paper or aluminum cup. As with larger cakes, frosting, icing and various other cake decorations such as fruit and candy may be applied."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Cupcakes%2C_chocolate_and_strawberry_flavour.jpg/330px-Cupcakes%2C_chocolate_and_strawberry_flavour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cupcake"},{"title":"Rose","blocks":[{"text":"A rose is either a woody perennial flowering plant of the genus Rosa, in the family Rosaceae, or the flower it bears. There are over three hundred species and tens of thousands of cultivars. The plants range in size and form, from trailing and erect shrubs to climbers up to 7 metres (23 ft) in height. Sharp prickles appear on the stems of many species. Their flowers vary in size and shape and are usually large and showy, in colours ranging from white through pinks, reds, oranges and yellows."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg/330px-Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose"},{"title":"Rose (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Rose is the color halfway between red and magenta, whose hue corresponds to an angle of 330 degrees on the HSV/HSL color wheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg/330px-Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Unfrosted_Cupcakes.jpg/500px-Unfrosted_Cupcakes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Unfrosted_Cupcakes.jpg/1280px-Unfrosted_Cupcakes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Unfrosted_Cupcakes.jpg/500px-Unfrosted_Cupcakes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Unfrosted cupcakes","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUnfrosted_Cupcakes.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Hostess-Cupcake-Whole.jpg/500px-Hostess-Cupcake-Whole.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Hostess-Cupcake-Whole.jpg/1280px-Hostess-Cupcake-Whole.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Hostess-Cupcake-Whole.jpg/500px-Hostess-Cupcake-Whole.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A mass-produced Hostess CupCake, which is branded as a \"snack cake\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHostess-Cupcake-Whole.j